{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ה' אלהיך הוא עובר לפניך", :translit "Hashem Elokekha hu oveir lifanekha", :gloss "YHWH your Elohim, He passes before you"} {:he "הפ' מתחיל ומסיים בשם", :translit "ha-parashah matchil u'msayeim ba-shem", :gloss "the passage begins and ends with the Name"} {:he "לומר שהקב\"ה הולך לפני ישראל ולאחריהם", :translit "lomar she-ha-Kadosh Barukh Hu holeikh lifnei Yisrael u'le'achareihem", :gloss "to say that the Holy One blessed be He walks before Israel and after them"} {:he "כי הולך לפניכם ה' ומאספכם אלהי ישראל", :translit "ki holeikh lifneikhem Hashem u'm'asefkhem Elohei Yisrael", :gloss "for He goes before you YHWH and gathers you Elohei Yisrael"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Literary framing: the parashah opens and closes with the divine Name, signifying God surrounds Israel both before and after."}], :frame {:text "Isaiah 52:12 states \"for YHWH goes before you, and the God of Israel is your rear guard,\" describing God leading Israel at the exodus from Egypt. Ba'al HaTurim reads the literary frame of this parashah — beginning and ending with the divine Name — as a structural echo of this verse's double movement: God both leads and follows Israel.", :sources ["Isaiah 52:12"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Literary framing: the parashah opens and closes with the divine Name, signifying God surrounds Israel both before and after.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:40:35.272872084Z", :model "glm-5.2"}